  "$comment": [
    "The four demo households, one place. Each is an IRS scenario (base) with the keys below changed",
    "(overrides): a Virginian's name, address and employer, the residence state, and the answers to the",
    "Virginia questions. scripts/virginia-demos.py build writes scenarios/<file>.json from this; check",
    "fails if a committed file differs. expect is what the engine alone computes for each (VirginiaSpec",
    "pins it; Lines 20 to 22 come from the records stand-in on the page, so the page's result differs);",
    "result is what the page shows. Read by: virginia-demo-link.js (?demo=N), virginia-demos.py (links,",
    "build, check), virginia-cases.py (the demos join the 50 households), virginia-a11y.cjs (demo 1 is",
    "the household it scans with), VirginiaSpec.scala (expect), virginia-stats.py --check (result)."
